# stops file for azino organ
#Format: name:pitch:scale:waveform:stopped:mems
# pitch: 1 is 8' (unison)
# (phasor forms instead use semitones above 64')
# scale: <1 for flute, ~1 for diapason, >1 for string
# (for waveform over it's instead a geometric ratio, so 0.2-0.5 or so)
# (for waveform chimney it's the scaling of even harmonics)
# waveform: 0=sine 1=triangle 2=explog 3=distortion
# w/phasors: 4=sine 5=vox 6=triangle 7=voxtri 8=reed 9=over 10=chimney
# stopped: boolean (effect is to have harmonics 1+3 instead of 1+2)
# mems: byte (8 bools), in which memories is this stop open by default?
# trailing ":groupname" marks the end of a group

